      "alt": "A architecture diagram titled \"SEARCH + AGENT INFERENCE RUN LOCALLY\" illustrating the interaction between a cloud-based coding agent and a local search agent system.\n * Coding Agent (Left Box): Represents a frontier LLM in the cloud (such as Claude Code, Codex, or OpenCode). A label underneath states \"34% fewer API tokens on code-search questions.\"\n * Local System Container (Dashed Box): Encloses two main components:\n   * ColGrep-Agent-2B (Middle Solid Blue Box): A 2B search agent using llama.cpp with a 2.5 GB GGUF model. It receives a \"question\" arrow from the Coding Agent and returns \"locations + code\" back to the Coding Agent.\n   * ColGrep (Right Box): Provides semantic search over a local index. It communicates back and forth with ColGrep-Agent-2B via multiple horizontal arrows labeled \"search, read, repeat.\"\n",
